WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.467
Over fifteen billion
miles away,

2
00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:05.967
Voyager One was sending
signals nobody could read.

3
00:00:06.233 --> 00:00:07.833
The trouble began in

4
00:00:07.833 --> 00:00:09.333
November
twenty twenty-three:

5
00:00:09.333 --> 00:00:10.900
a failed memory chip

6
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.133
in its data-packaging
computer.

7
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.600
Engineers couldn't
repair the chip.

8
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.800
So they moved
the affected code.

9
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.267
But it wouldn't fit
in one place.

10
00:00:20.733 --> 00:00:23.033
They split it
across working memory,

11
00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:25.000
then updated the instructions

12
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.167
so the pieces
still worked together.

13
00:00:27.633 --> 00:00:30.833
A command took about
twenty-two and a half hours

14
00:00:30.833 --> 00:00:32.500
just to reach the spacecraft.

15
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.867
On April twentieth,
twenty twenty-four,

16
00:00:35.867 --> 00:00:38.300
readable engineering data
came back.

17
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.167
Science data followed later.

18
00:00:40.533 --> 00:00:42.233
The chip stayed broken.

19
00:00:42.233 --> 00:00:44.167
The software worked around it.
